@startuml integrity-validation-pipeline
' Integrity constraints and where each is enforced across the campaign.
' Companion to docs/benchmarks/cross-language/methodology.md §4-§5.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam roundcorner 8

skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
}

' Colour legend, applied consistently:
'   blue   = preparation / provenance capture
'   green  = correctness gating
'   amber  = measurement under constraint
'   purple = post-hoc integrity analysis
'   red    = abort / quarantine paths

title Integrity constraints and their enforcement points

|#E3F2FD|preparation|
start
:**env-capture**
pins SHA-256 of every artifact:
cdylibs, dictionary, query sets,
vendored legacy bundles;
note right #E3F2FD
  Establishes the run's identity.
  Every later check compares
  against these pins.
end note

:**doctor**
governor = performance on cpus 2-9,
SMT siblings idle, release cdylibs
present, per-toolchain smoke test;
if (all requested targets ready?) then (no)
  :**ABORT**
  a target that cannot run is never
  silently skipped; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#E8F5E9|correctness gate|
:**gate.py**
every target vs the Rust oracle
over the verify-cell family;
:compare the four-tuple
<latex>(\,|M|,\ \sum |t|,\ \sum d,\ \mathrm{FNV}\text{-}1a_{64}\,)</latex>;
if (bit-exact for every target?) then (no)
  :**ABORT**
  timing is never accepted from an
  implementation that is not proven
  correct on this workload; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#FFF8E1|measurement (strictly serial)|
repeat :next cell;
  :snapshot cpu MHz + load_avg_1m;
  :**taskset** pin
  single-threaded: cpu 2
  managed runtimes: cpus 2-9
  (identical for both arms of a pair);
  :warm up <latex>\geq 3</latex> s, then pin the
  reference pair <latex>(|M|, \mathrm{checksum})</latex>;
  repeat :timed pass <latex>i</latex>;
    :drain every cursor fully,
    materialize <latex>(term, distance)</latex>;
    if (pass reproduces the reference?) then (no)
      :**FAIL THE CELL**
      nondeterminism is never
      averaged away; <<#FFCDD2>>
      stop
    else (yes)
    endif
  repeat while (more samples?) is (yes)
  ->no;
  :**postfill**
  run_id, environment_ref, cell_snapshot,
  workload digests, **native_digests**;
  if (cell validates against the schema?) then (no)
    :**QUARANTINE**
    incomplete record moved aside
    with a manifest; resume
    re-measures the coordinate; <<#FFCDD2>>
    detach
  else (yes)
  endif
  :cell written;
  note right #FFF8E1
    Concurrently, the **timed-process guard**
    classifies every harness process as
    MINE / FOREIGN / WRAPPER and ledgers
    foreign intervals <latex>[\,started,\ ended\_by\,]</latex>.
  end note
  if (drift sentinel due?) then (yes)
    :re-run 3 fixed anchor cells;
    if (median shift > 5%?) then (yes)
      :annotate the window; <<#FFE0B2>>
    else (no)
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
repeat while (more cells?) is (yes)
->no;

|#F3E5F5|post-hoc integrity analysis|
:**mark-contended-cells**
reconstruct each cell's window
<latex>t_{start} = t_{stamp} - (\sum_i s_i + w + c)</latex>
and intersect with foreign intervals;
:stamp <latex>contended = true</latex>
(declared in the schema, so flagged
cells are never dropped as invalid);

:**aggregate**
check digest consistency;
if (all workload + native digests match the pins?) then (no)
  :**ABORT**
  refuse to summarize a run whose
  cells measured different binaries
  or different inputs; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:robust statistics per cell
median, MAD, p10/p90,
bootstrap 95% CI of the median
(10 000 resamples, seed 42);
:ratios summarized **geometrically**
<latex>\bar{r} = \exp\!\big(\tfrac{1}{n}\sum_i \ln r_i\big)</latex>;
:emit summary.json + tables/
including contention.md and
the mandatory "not measured" table;

|#E1F5FE|system of record|
:**publish to pgmcp**
content-addressed, idempotent;
:experiments decided against
**preregistered** criteria
(refutations published as refutations);
stop

legend right
  |= colour |= stage |
  |<#E3F2FD>| preparation / provenance |
  |<#E8F5E9>| correctness gating |
  |<#FFF8E1>| measurement under constraint |
  |<#F3E5F5>| post-hoc integrity analysis |
  |<#E1F5FE>| system of record |
  |<#FFCDD2>| abort / quarantine |
endlegend

@enduml
